From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Add FT (Fast BSS Transition) support for non-AP MLDs

FT authentication and reassociation from a non-AP MLD were not handled:
the FT Authentication frame was not recognized as an MLO frame (so the
STA entry used the link address and no Basic Multi-Link element was
returned), the PMK-R0/PMK-R1/PTK derivation used the link addresses
instead of the MLD MAC addresses, the R1KH-ID defaulted to the per-link
BSSID, and the FTE MIC calculation and the group key subelements in the
Reassociation Response frame followed the non-MLO rules.

Implement the AP MLD side of FT over-the-air per IEEE Std 802.11be:
- recognize FT Authentication frames from non-AP MLDs and set the ML
  information in the RSN authenticator before the PTK is derived
- use the MLD MAC addresses (SPA/AA) in PMK-R0, PMK-R1, PMKR1Name, and
  PTK derivation
- default the R1KH-ID of an AP MLD to the AP MLD MAC address on all
  affiliated links
- include the non-AP MLD link addresses in the Reassociation Request
  frame FTE MIC (13.8.4) and the affiliated AP RSNEs/RSNXEs and BSSIDs in
  the Reassociation Response frame FTE MIC with the matching element
  count (13.8.5)
- deliver per-link group keys with the MLO GTK/IGTK/BIGTK subelements

The rules follow the wlantest implementation of the same calculations.
FT over-the-DS with AP MLDs is not changed.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
